# Windsurf Cascade — Persistent Coding Rules
# These rules apply to every session in this project.

## Imports
- All imports must be at the top of the file, never inline
- Use absolute imports from `src/` (e.g. `from src.models.schema import OutputRow`)

## Types
- Type hints required on ALL function signatures (parameters and return types)
- Use `TypedDict` for DataFrame column contracts; reference `src/models/schema.py`
- Prefer `pd.DataFrame` with column validation over untyped dicts

## Style
- ruff formatting enforced — line length 100
- No magic numbers; all constants in `configs/` YAML files
- Use `logging` module, never `print()`
- Docstrings on all public functions: one-line summary + Args + Returns

## Testing
- Every new model function gets at least one pytest test before the PR
- Tests live in `tests/` mirroring `src/` structure
- Use fixtures from `tests/conftest.py` — never hardcode test data inline
- Plausibility checks must be automated, not manual

## Data / DuckDB
- All gold table writes go through `src/data/gold_writer.py`
- Every gold table must have: `source_id`, `ingestion_date`, `version`, `run_id` columns
- Never write raw files to `data/gold/` directly — always via the writer

## Schema Contract
- NEVER change column names or types in `src/models/schema.py` without a migration
- All model functions must return DataFrames validated against `OutputSchema`
- `confidence_tier` must be 1, 2, or 3 — never null
- `run_id` must be a UUID string — never null

## Streamlit
- `app/` imports from `src/` only — no model logic in Streamlit pages
- Use `st.cache_data` for all expensive computations
- All charts use Plotly — no matplotlib in the app

## Git
- Commit messages: `type(scope): description` (e.g. `feat(dc-model): add PUE trajectory`)
- Never commit to main directly — use feature branches
